  "faqEyebrow": "Questions",
  "faqTitle": "Good to know",
  "faq1Q": "Do I need an AI key?",
  "faq1A": "No. On a phone, download a model once in Account → AI & voice and the coach works offline. A key from Groq, Gemini, OpenAI or another provider gives stronger answers; free tiers exist at Groq, Gemini and OpenRouter. In a web browser the on-device models can’t run, so the web version needs your key for the coach.",
  "faq2Q": "Which levels and exams does it cover?",
  "faq2A": "48 lessons from Pre-A1 to B2, with exam tracks for Goethe-Zertifikat A1, A2, B1 and B2 and for TestDaF, plus mock exams.",
  "faq3Q": "Does it work offline?",
  "faq3A": "Lessons, saved words, reviews and your progress work offline. The coach works offline too when you use a model on your phone. Your own AI key and syncing need the internet.",
  "faq4Q": "What language explains German?",
  "faq4A": "You choose during onboarding: English, Hindi or Telugu, or Other.",
  "faq5Q": "Are my conversations used to train AI?",
  "faq5A": "Not by Sprichst. On your phone they stay on your phone. With your own key, your messages go to the provider you chose under your own agreement with them. Sprichst never receives them.",
  "faq6Q": "Can I delete my data?",
  "faq6A": "Yes. Export everything as JSON or erase your account in Account → Privacy & data.",
  "faq7Q": "Is it accessible?",
  "faq7A": "Light and dark themes checked for WCAG AA contrast, 48-pixel touch targets, text that follows your device’s text size, and animations that stop when Reduce Motion is on.",

